Description: SRUM database (SrumECmd)
Category: SRUM
Author: ArtefactForge
Version: '1.1'
ExportFormat: csv
OutputName: SrumECmd
# -r SOFTWARE is optional but strongly recommended: it resolves app and user IDs.
#
# SrumECmd opens SRUDB.dat through Windows' own ESE engine, which replays the transaction logs into
# the database and rewrites SRUDB.dat, SRUDB.jfm, SRU.chk and SRU.log in place. Measured on a
# collected sru folder: all four changed hash after one run. So the whole sru folder is copied into
# %workDir% first and SrumECmd only ever sees the copy. The log replay still happens, on the copy,
# so the output is the same as before. %workDir% is scratch space, deleted when the module finishes.
#
# The copy is not ContinueOnError: if it fails, the module fails and is flagged for review rather
# than falling back to opening the evidence. SOFTWARE is read through the registry library, which
# does not write, so it is passed from the evidence as-is.
#
# SrumECmd's own replay is not enough for a database collected while Windows had it open, which
# is how Velociraptor collects it: on such a copy it failed with "Access denied" / "not shut down
# cleanly" and wrote nothing. So the copy is recovered first with esentutl /r, the way Windows
# would. The log and system paths are given explicitly and /i is NOT used: with /i the recovery
# reported success but left the database dirty. A clean database needs no recovery and esentutl
# leaves it alone. If the logs were not collected, recovery fails (ContinueOnError) and SrumECmd
# then reports the dirty database, so the module is flagged rather than repaired with /p, which
# discards data.
#
# Live systems use SrumECmd_Live, which stages through a shadow copy instead.
Requires: ['%root%\Windows\System32\sru\SRUDB.dat']
Scope: offlineonly
Platform: windows
Priority: 60
IoWeight: heavy

Prepare:
  -
    Executable: C:\Windows\System32\cmd.exe
    CommandLine: /c copy /y /b "%root%\Windows\System32\sru\*" "%workDir%\"
  -
    Executable: C:\Windows\System32\esentutl.exe
    CommandLine: /r sru /l . /s . /d .
    WorkingDirectory: '%workDir%'
    ContinueOnError: true

Processors:
  -
    Executable: eztools\SrumECmd.exe
    CommandLine: -f "%workDir%\SRUDB.dat" -r "%root%\Windows\System32\config\SOFTWARE" --csv "%destinationDirectory%"
    ExportFormat: csv
